    "body": "### Problem\n\nContinuous update of visual selection in multicursor with enabled ui2 causes flicker.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean`\n2. `:lua require('vim._core.ui2').enable({ enable = true })`\n3. `:e LICENSE.txt` (from the root of this repo)\n4. Type `V3j` - `Q` - `v` to start multicursor and visual select.\n5. Continuously press `l` until no selection update, then `h`, then `j`, etc. At some point the selection update start to flicker, like if there is forced redraw without highlighting from extmarks. This doesn't seem to happen without ui2 enabled.\n\nA demo (flickering start at around 00:20):\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/94bff434-2f39-4b82-9213-123f56a872d6\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nEnabling ui2 should not cause flicker with visual selection while multicursor is active.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1499+gb51a0b2dcc\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, doesn't have this functionality\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.1.11-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage and from source",
